{
  "description": "ScVal recursion and boundary vectors derived from stellar-xdr 28.0.1 and Stellar-contract.x. The crate has no protocol-level fixed nesting ceiling: Limits::none() sets depth to u32::MAX and callers choose Limits::depth(n). The configured boundary below is therefore an explicit decoder-limit exercise, not an invented Soroban or protocol rule.",
  "source_reference": "https://github.com/stellar/rs-stellar-xdr/tree/v28.0.1/stellar-xdr",
  "xdr_definition_reference": "https://github.com/stellar/stellar-xdr/blob/9c9c145953e80990d6ff1ae3a6a973a0ce6d0694/Stellar-contract.x",
  "crate": {
    "name": "stellar-xdr",
    "version": "28.0.1",
    "limits_none_depth": 4294967295,
    "configured_limits_depth": 67,
    "configured_container_depth": 16,
    "depth_accounting": "For a one-element nested Vec, the generated ScVal, Option<ScVec>, ScVec and VecM readers each consume one depth; the leaf ScVal requires three more, so Limits::depth(67) accepts 16 container layers and rejects the 17th."
  },
